archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3124,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/pulls/7804","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/7804","diff_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/7804.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/7804.patch","merged_at":"2019-10-29T14:05:45Z"},"body":"Fix #7800 \r\n\r\nMost of this code is yanked from the standard library since the same behaviors are desired, just with plumbing for `stdout`/`stderr`. One difference of note is that `version` is mandatory in `CapturableVersionAction.__init__` to get around this error:\r\n```\r\nmypy/main.py:339: error: \"ArgumentParser\" has no attribute \"version\"  [attr-defined]\r\n                version = parser.version\r\n                          ^\r\n```\r\nI'm unaware of a situation where [that line](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/955f96f6aae7c1a54d88c3f7a51c2e142ac7e4d4/Lib/argparse.py#L1067) wouldn't raise an `AttributeError` 🤔 \r\nAnyways, I didn't want to patch `sys.stdout`/`sys.stderr` in order to avoid reintroducing #6125.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/7804/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/7804/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":2748241820,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI3NDgyNDE4MjA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/2748241820",